{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/946462-convention-vs-home-games","id":946462,"title":"Convention vs home games..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-08T14:30:55-07:00","id":946462,"title":"Convention vs home games..","content":"Not sure if this is the proper sub-forum for it (or convention/gatherings would be), but here goes..<br /> <br /> Had a situation Friday crop up, where a player commented to me, that he feels PC's in rpgs should be somewhat 'immune' to dying off early in a gaming session (say before hour 2 of a 4 hr slot), just so that said player should feel he at least got &quot;His money's worth&quot; from the event..<br /> Talking on a smoke break with some of the Shadowrun/pathfinder/b.tech people i saw outside, i got a varied response from them when i put HIS comment to them as a question..<br /> So SHOULD a player, have some sort of expectation, that if he say pays for a 4 hr slot of gaming, but something goes real bad early on (they get into combat when they shouldn't have, dice rolls go pear shaped etc), that they shouldn't die before say the halfway mark??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-08T20:10:24-07:00","id":946700,"title":"","content":"My general style as an ST when running convention games is a more compressed version of my guidelines for a campaign game.<br /> <br /> Player Characters should not die die JUST to a few bad rolls.<br /> <br /> If someone makes a Dramatic Last Stand kind of thing fine, but bad rolls should present challenges to the character rather than cripple them.<br /> <br /> There's a few corner cases where it's a bit different... a thing where after players die they rise as undead that then dedicate themselves to hunting down the remaining party members, I'd allow cheap deaths there because it's just a change, not an end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T00:46:09-07:00","id":949172,"title":"","content":"You do something dumb. You get hurt. You do something monumentally dumb. You die.<br /> If you've any attachment to your character, avoid being dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T10:54:10-07:00","id":949412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/946462-convention-vs-home-games?p=949172#post949172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do something dumb. You get hurt. You do something monumentally dumb. You die.<br /> If you've any attachment to your character, avoid being dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This. I don't aim to kill characters. If you do something that is dumb and will lead to your character's death, I'm going to warn you first.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you sure you want to pet the Dragon behind its ear?&quot;<br /> &quot;Yeah!&quot;<br /> &quot;This is an ancient dragon. Petting it behind its 'ears' would be suicidal.&quot;<br /> &quot;I got Acrobatics.&quot;<br /> &quot;Okay... Well, the Dragon wakes up. I'll let you live if you roll a natural 20.&quot;<br /> &quot;What, what? You killed my character!&quot;<br /> &quot;What part of 'suicidal' did you not understand?!?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T13:09:49-07:00","id":949481,"title":"","content":"Of the # of deaths i have had in my SW gaming at conventions, some of the stupider ones were<br /> A) a bounty hunter using his jet pack to fly through a smoke field into a KNOWN thick forested area, hoping to get near the enemy so he could brawl.. Made such a poor Jet pac operations roll, he damn near killed himself going head first INTO one of those trees.. While on the ground shaking his head clear of the cobwebs, one of the enemies i CLEARLY described as shooting his JET PACK (not him.. And what does the guy do..?! He jet packs BACK to the party taking a 2 round arching route. Jetpack goes boom right as he landed...<br /> <br /> B) Two pcs ona speeder bike one carrying a large backpack of explosives going DOUBLE speed (again through a smoke field) slap bank into a building.. Bike blew up both went to mortally wounded from the explosion.. THEN the one pc mentions &quot;So what about all the explosives i am carrying??&quot;..<br /> <br /> C) Twin seat Y-wing fleeing a group of modified Tie fighters (Switched for Ion cannons for pirate capture), right into a large asteroid field.. Pilot decides he wants to go FLANK Speed (thus would not get a dodge roll if shot at), to try and gain distance on said Ties.. RIGHT towards a large asteroid he said &quot;i will get as close as possible then try to skirt RIGHT along its surface, using my repulsors to keep me just above the ground of it..<br /> GETS hit three times before getting ot the asteroid, shutting his ship down.. However he STILL had that flank speed momentum, which caried it in, and thus crashed... Fighter blew up. One of the 2 in the ship, mortally wounded, one dead.. The one at MW died from exposure before any imps got to him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11674-garhkal","name":"garhkal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11674_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"547"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T14:22:00-07:00","id":949531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Revenge of TV Head</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/946462-convention-vs-home-games?p=949172#post949172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do something dumb. You get hurt. You do something monumentally dumb. You die.<br /> If you've any attachment to your character, avoid being dumb.</div> </div> </div> </div>This times 50.<br /> <br /> I ended a Hunter: the Reckoning game after 3 sessions because the players were too accustomed to playing difficult-to-kill vampires, werewolves and mages. Changing gears to squishy humans was a bit much for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T11:09:56-07:00","id":950649,"title":"","content":"Some people are new to games. I feel people should be given more leeway and while still punished, it shouldn't be an outright kill just because they don't fully get it. People sometimes act dumb when new to games, but with a little patience some of them have become some of the most avid RPGers. I feel like convention games are for the public or to introduce games, so require more kid gloves then usual games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}